<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Crisis</p><h1 class="enc-title">The Emergency (India)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1975–1977</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Emergency was a period from June 1975 to March 1977 during which Prime Minister <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indira-gandhi">Indira Gandhi</a> ruled by decree after a court found her guilty of electoral malpractice. Civil liberties were suspended, the press was censored, opposition leaders were jailed and a forced sterilisation campaign was carried out. When elections were held in 1977, voters rejected <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahatma-gandhi">Gandhi</a> and brought the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/janata-party">Janata Party</a> to power.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/the-emergency-india.jpg" alt="The Emergency (India)" width="320" height="211" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown, dedicated to Bettmann Archive · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Indira_Gandhi_1966.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
